1
00:02:46,767 --> 00:02:49,407
Yes, ma'am,
how ya doin'?

2
00:02:49,470 --> 00:02:51,780
Is this Rose Hill?

3
00:02:51,839 --> 00:02:54,410
Good,
This is Ed Couch.

4
00:02:54,475 --> 00:02:56,921
I'm Vesta Adcock's nephew.

5
00:02:56,978 --> 00:02:59,219
I need to get up there
and see her,

6
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:03,285
but I'm gonna be late
'cause I'm lost out here.

7
00:03:03,351 --> 00:03:05,831
We're off the Alabama interstate
but I don't know where.

8
00:03:42,256 --> 00:03:46,170
- Did you hear that?
- What?

9
00:03:46,227 --> 00:03:48,298
The train.

10
00:03:48,362 --> 00:03:51,241
No, I didn't hear
no train.

11
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,344
Oh, nothin',
I guess.

12
00:03:55,403 --> 00:03:59,818
- Where's "Whistle Stop"
on the map?
- I can't find it.

13
00:03:59,874 --> 00:04:03,754
Why did you tell me to
turn right 10 miles back there?

14
00:04:05,279 --> 00:04:08,817
God, you got a negative
sense of direction, hon.

15
00:04:08,883 --> 00:04:11,762
I'm sorry.

16
00:04:11,819 --> 00:04:16,029
Oh, Ed,your aunt's gonna be
so disappointed we're late.

17
00:04:16,090 --> 00:04:20,095
I know she's
been looking forward to
this visit all week long.

18
00:04:20,161 --> 00:04:23,438
Bless her sweet,
little ol' heart.

19
00:04:27,568 --> 00:04:30,447
Hey, how's my sweet Auntie V
this afternoon?

20
00:04:30,504 --> 00:04:33,110
Remember us?

21
00:04:33,174 --> 00:04:36,246
- Don't you look pretty!
- We brought you something.

22
00:04:36,310 --> 00:04:39,484
- Let me look at you.

23
00:04:39,547 --> 00:04:42,153
Don't you know
Evelyn loves you?

24
00:04:42,216 --> 00:04:47,063
Well, honey,
I guess it'd be better if
you wait out here for me.

25
00:04:47,121 --> 00:04:51,592
-I'll get all this stuff.
- Well, if you think it's best.

26
00:04:51,659 --> 00:04:54,970
Yeah, I do this time.
Okay?

27
00:04:55,029 --> 00:04:57,202
Have a nice day,
Aunt Vesta.

28
00:04:57,265 --> 00:04:59,211
Don't you pitch a fit
like that'

29
00:05:11,178 --> 00:05:13,886
Did you know
they took my gallbladder out?

30
00:05:15,316 --> 00:05:17,455
No, I didn't.

31
00:05:17,518 --> 00:05:21,193
Oh, yes. Still
in the hospital in ajar.

32
00:05:21,255 --> 00:05:26,068
I guess that's where
they keep 'em.

33
00:05:26,127 --> 00:05:28,107
I guess.

34
00:05:28,162 --> 00:05:30,403
When I was
in the hospital,

35
00:05:30,464 --> 00:05:34,435
the nurse gave me one of them
Fleet enemas they're so fond of.

36
00:05:34,502 --> 00:05:37,108
Mrs. Cleo Threadgoode,

37
00:05:37,171 --> 00:05:40,482
82 year old widow,
imagine that.

38
00:05:40,541 --> 00:05:43,681
Actually,
everybody calls me Ninny.

39
00:05:43,744 --> 00:05:45,985
'Course I'm
just visitin' here.

40
00:05:46,047 --> 00:05:51,326
Did you ever have
one of them Fleet enemas?

41
00:05:51,385 --> 00:05:53,331
Um,well?

42
00:05:53,387 --> 00:05:55,458
No.

43
00:05:55,523 --> 00:05:58,766
You'd remember it.

44
00:05:58,826 --> 00:06:02,501
Me and my friend, Mrs. Otis,
come from Whistle Stop.

45
00:06:02,563 --> 00:06:04,770
You ever been
to Whistle Stop?

46
00:06:04,832 --> 00:06:08,245
Why, yes. I just
passed by there today.

47
00:06:08,302 --> 00:06:13,183
She's lived
down the street from me
for 30 years or more.

48
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:15,242
After her son died,

49
00:06:15,309 --> 00:06:18,916
her daughter-in-law had a fit
for her to come live
at the nursing home.

50
00:06:18,979 --> 00:06:22,290
They asked me to come
and be her roommate.

51
00:06:22,350 --> 00:06:26,594
Mrs. Otis don't know it,
but I'm going home just soon
as she gets settled in good.

52
00:06:28,923 --> 00:06:32,336
Does the name
"Idgie Threadgoode"
ring a bell?

53
00:06:32,393 --> 00:06:35,931
Um, no, ma'am.
I don't think so.

54
00:06:35,996 --> 00:06:38,806
You'd remember her.

55
00:06:38,866 --> 00:06:42,780
You see,
I was practically adopted
by the Threadgoode family.

56
00:06:42,837 --> 00:06:45,181
- I married her brother, Cleo.
- Oh, uh-huh.

57
00:06:48,533 --> 00:06:50,033
[Edit: Ninny: gossip that anyone thought Idgie murdered “that man.”]

58
00:06:50,219 --> 00:06:52,859
Oh, now, let's see.

59
00:06:52,922 --> 00:06:56,392
I 'member the day they pulled
that truck up out of the river.

60
00:06:57,542 --> 00:07:01,042
[Edit: Idgie arrested for the murder of Frank Bennett; “start with Buddy.”]

61
00:07:03,783 --> 00:07:07,560
I 'member the day we
was all gettin' ready
for Leona's weddin'.

62
00:07:07,620 --> 00:07:09,600
The war had just ended,

63
00:07:09,655 --> 00:07:11,999
the Great one,
you know.

64
00:07:12,058 --> 00:07:16,734
And another one
was about to begin in
the Threadgoode house.

65
00:07:16,796 --> 00:07:19,242
Sipsey hone )4
is that finished?

66
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:23,747
- Buddy,
get dressed honey.
- Mama?

67
00:07:23,803 --> 00:07:25,783
Leona, what is it?

68
00:07:25,838 --> 00:07:27,715
Idgie's upstairs
in her room...

69
00:07:27,774 --> 00:07:29,754
and says she won't come out
as long as she lives.

70
00:07:29,809 --> 00:07:31,948
- She is gonna ruin my weddin'!
- Shh.

71
00:07:32,011 --> 00:07:34,821
Leona, you're gonna be
the most beautiful bride.

72
00:07:34,881 --> 00:07:38,158
Of course she is, Papa.

73
00:07:38,217 --> 00:07:42,165
Your papa has spent
every last nickel he has
just to make you happy.

74
00:07:42,221 --> 00:07:46,033
Now, you try to act
a little grateful, young lady.

75
00:07:46,092 --> 00:07:49,198
Imogene Louise Threadgoode!

76
00:07:49,262 --> 00:07:51,799
This is your mama!

77
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:59,149
You come down here right now.
Do you hear me?

78
00:07:59,205 --> 00:08:01,845
- Buddy, fetch her.
She'll listen to you.
- Come on down, little bit.

79
00:08:01,908 --> 00:08:04,479
There's no firin'
squad waitin' for you.

80
00:08:04,544 --> 00:08:09,892
Ohh! Come on, honey
Let us see you.

81
00:08:09,949 --> 00:08:12,122
You look so pretty.

82
00:08:12,185 --> 00:08:15,029
- I see London,
I see-
- Hush!

83
00:08:16,756 --> 00:08:20,203
Julian, hush.

84
00:08:20,259 --> 00:08:23,001
Come ahead, sweetheart.

85
00:08:23,062 --> 00:08:26,805
You look awful nice
in that.

86
00:08:26,866 --> 00:08:28,470
- Mama!
- You look fine.

87
00:08:28,534 --> 00:08:31,037
She looks like a monkey

88
00:08:31,104 --> 00:08:32,913
Julian, stop it
right this second!

89
00:08:32,972 --> 00:08:36,317
Take it back!
Take it back!
Idgie, hey!

90
00:08:36,375 --> 00:08:39,481
I told you she
was gonna ruin my weddin'!

91
00:08:39,545 --> 00:08:41,923
- Idgie, get up.
- Take it back!

92
00:08:41,981 --> 00:08:44,154
Take it back!

93
00:08:44,217 --> 00:08:47,562
- I'll get you for this.
- No, Buddy.

94
00:08:51,357 --> 00:08:54,429
We have to be careful
when she's dressing up.

95
00:08:54,494 --> 00:08:56,440
She's just a pain!

96
00:08:56,496 --> 00:09:00,034
Leona, will you
stop shrieking'

97
00:09:00,099 --> 00:09:02,807
This is your
weddin ' day'

98
00:09:13,813 --> 00:09:16,657
I oaks like you got yourself
up a tree, little bit.

99
00:09:16,716 --> 00:09:19,754
I'm sick of people
makin' fun of me.

100
00:09:19,819 --> 00:09:22,356
So you're gonna stay up here
all day long.

101
00:09:22,421 --> 00:09:25,630
Yep.
The hell with them.

102
00:09:25,691 --> 00:09:29,639
Who wants to wear
that stupid ol' dress anyway?

103
00:09:29,695 --> 00:09:33,074
- I ever tell you about the oysters?
- Oysters?

104
00:09:33,132 --> 00:09:35,078
- I tell you about the oysters?
- No.

105
00:09:35,134 --> 00:09:39,810
Think about the millions of
oysters lyin' around the ocean.

106
00:09:39,872 --> 00:09:42,216
Then one day...

107
00:09:42,275 --> 00:09:45,085
God comes along and sees one
and he says,

108
00:09:45,144 --> 00:09:48,057
"I think I'm gonna make
that one different."

109
00:09:48,114 --> 00:09:50,321
You know what he does?

110
00:09:50,383 --> 00:09:53,557
He puts a little
piece of sand in it.

111
00:09:53,619 --> 00:09:57,863
- Guess what it can do
that the others can't.
- What?

112
00:09:57,924 --> 00:10:01,235
It can make
a beautiful pearl.

113
00:10:01,294 --> 00:10:03,467
What if God
made a mistake?

114
00:10:03,529 --> 00:10:08,638
Well, the way I figure it,
he never makes mistakes.

115
00:10:08,701 --> 00:10:11,477
I mean, he made sure
we got together.

116
00:10:11,537 --> 00:10:13,539
He made sure you got
the best looking,

117
00:10:13,606 --> 00:10:15,813
most charmin' brother
in the world...

118
00:10:15,875 --> 00:10:19,254
- who's gonna beat you
to the chocolate cake.
- You will not.

119
00:10:19,312 --> 00:10:21,690
Got you out of the tree,
didn't I?

120
00:10:21,747 --> 00:10:24,694
Did not!

121
00:10:24,750 --> 00:10:28,391
Into this estate,
these two come now to be joined

122
00:10:28,454 --> 00:10:30,559
If any man present
can show cause...

123
00:10:30,623 --> 00:10:33,035
why they may not lawfully
be joined together,

124
00:10:33,092 --> 00:10:38,235
let him speak now or
forever after hold his peace.

125
00:10:38,297 --> 00:10:40,971
Please be seated.

126
00:10:43,336 --> 00:10:45,543
If either of you
know any reason...

127
00:10:45,605 --> 00:10:48,586
why you may not justly
be joined together
in holy matrimony

128
00:10:48,641 --> 00:10:51,121
do you now confess it?

129
00:11:00,753 --> 00:11:03,461
It is then your will
to proceed.

130
00:11:03,522 --> 00:11:07,231
Do you,
Charles Osgood justice-

131
00:11:13,065 --> 00:11:16,410
Thank you. I don't know what
we'd do without your generosity.

132
00:11:16,469 --> 00:11:19,450
Sipsey, especially you.
Look what you've clone!

133
00:11:19,505 --> 00:11:23,453
Thank you, Mrs. Threadgoode.
Gimme that, you rascal!

134
00:11:27,780 --> 00:11:30,351
John!
Jump on my back

135
00:11:30,416 --> 00:11:34,057
I don't think
there ever was a sweeter boy
than Buddy Threadgoode.

136
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:38,626
- You look beautiful, Lily.
- Yes, Lily, you sure do.

137
00:11:38,691 --> 00:11:42,138
I had the biggest crush
on him.

138
00:11:42,194 --> 00:11:44,538
He was a terrible flirt!

139
00:11:44,597 --> 00:11:47,840
But his heart belonged
to Ruth Jamison.

140
00:11:47,900 --> 00:11:51,074
She was the daughter of
a friend of his mama's...

141
00:11:51,137 --> 00:11:53,947
who was visitin'
that summer.

142
00:11:54,006 --> 00:11:57,476
Ruth Jamison,
you're just the one
I've been lookin' for.

143
00:11:57,543 --> 00:12:00,649
- Are you thirsty?
- Let's go visit
someplace else.

144
00:12:06,552 --> 00:12:09,897
Think that's a big lake,
you should've seen the
one next to our house.

145
00:12:09,955 --> 00:12:12,094
We used to swim in it
and fish.

146
00:12:12,158 --> 00:12:14,832
I sure do miss it.
Sure do.

147
00:12:14,894 --> 00:12:17,636
What happened to it?
Did it dry up?

148
00:12:17,697 --> 00:12:19,643
No, worse than that.

149
00:12:19,699 --> 00:12:21,770
Last fall,
a ﬂock of ducks,

150
00:12:21,834 --> 00:12:26,112
40 or 50 of 'em,
landed right smack
in the middle of it.

151
00:12:26,172 --> 00:12:28,049
This ﬂuke thing
happened.

152
00:12:28,107 --> 00:12:30,587
The temperature dropped so fast
that the whole lake froze...

153
00:12:30,643 --> 00:12:32,645
in three seconds,
just like that!

154
00:12:32,712 --> 00:12:35,022
Those poor little ducks.
Did it kill them?

155
00:12:35,081 --> 00:12:38,290
No, they ﬂew off
and took the lake with 'em.

156
00:12:38,351 --> 00:12:41,730
To this very day, that lake
is somewhere over in Georgia.

157
00:12:41,787 --> 00:12:45,234
Buddy Threadgoode.

158
00:12:56,202 --> 00:12:59,547
Come a little closer.
I wanna give you something.

159
00:12:59,605 --> 00:13:02,051
Come here.

160
00:13:05,911 --> 00:13:08,152
Whoop!

161
00:13:12,284 --> 00:13:15,697
Come back here, hat. Where
do you think you're gain'?

162
00:13:17,923 --> 00:13:19,869
Whoa!

163
00:13:19,925 --> 00:13:23,031
I got it.
Hold on, Ruth.
Hold on, little bit.

164
00:13:27,433 --> 00:13:30,175
It's all right.
I got it.

165
00:13:32,304 --> 00:13:36,047
Come here,
you damn hat.
Got it!

166
00:13:36,108 --> 00:13:39,055
Oh, I meant
to do that.

167
00:13:40,112 --> 00:13:43,855
I... got it!

168
00:13:43,916 --> 00:13:45,793
Ta-da!

169
00:13:47,586 --> 00:13:50,123
All right.
Damn!

170
00:13:50,189 --> 00:13:52,169
Come on.

171
00:13:58,798 --> 00:14:03,679
Come on. Get out.
Get out.

172
00:14:03,736 --> 00:14:05,682
Buddy!

173
00:14:05,738 --> 00:14:08,981
- Buddy!
- Buddy Threadgoode!

174
00:14:10,609 --> 00:14:12,316
Come on, Buddy!

175
00:14:12,378 --> 00:14:14,119
Get out.

176
00:14:15,581 --> 00:14:17,720
Get out of there.

177
00:14:19,051 --> 00:14:22,863
Buddy!

178
00:14:22,922 --> 00:14:26,062
- Come on, Buddy!
- Buddy'

179
00:14:26,125 --> 00:14:28,731
Buddy!

180
00:14:31,263 --> 00:14:33,869
No-o-o!

181
00:14:33,933 --> 00:14:37,779
Buddy!

182
00:14:37,837 --> 00:14:41,250
Buddy, no!
No!

183
00:14:41,307 --> 00:14:44,083
No! Buddy!
No-o-o!

184
00:14:44,143 --> 00:14:47,181
No! Buddy!
Let me go!

185
00:14:48,647 --> 00:14:52,459
' No!
- Buddy!

186
00:14:52,518 --> 00:14:56,159
- You got to go back to the house.

187
00:14:56,222 --> 00:14:58,725
Come on.
We're gonna go home.

188
00:14:58,791 --> 00:15:01,635
- Buddy!
- You have to be strong.

189
00:15:01,694 --> 00:15:04,607
- It'll be okay.
- Buddy!

190
00:15:04,663 --> 00:15:07,610
"The Lord is my Shepherd,

191
00:15:07,666 --> 00:15:09,873
I shall not want."

192
00:15:09,935 --> 00:15:12,939
Oh, it like
to have killed us all

193
00:15:13,005 --> 00:15:15,679
But nary a one took it
as hard as Idgie,

194
00:15:18,777 --> 00:15:24,250
everyone thought she 'o' die
right along with him.

195
00:15:40,900 --> 00:15:45,178
Night alter night,
she stayed by the river.

196
00:15:45,237 --> 00:15:49,413
Big George was the only soul
she'd let near her,

197
00:15:49,475 --> 00:15:53,013
and he watched over her
night and day

198
00:15:53,078 --> 00:15:55,888
You know,
a heart can be broken,

199
00:15:55,948 --> 00:15:59,020
but it still keeps a-beatin'
just the same.

200
00:15:59,084 --> 00:16:01,724
Miss Idgie, you'll have
to keep this blanket on...

201
00:16:01,787 --> 00:16:04,700
or you'll catch
your death of cold,
you hear me now?

202
00:16:04,757 --> 00:16:09,172
That's so sad.

203
00:16:14,567 --> 00:16:17,173
Ah.

204
00:16:17,236 --> 00:16:19,238
Would you like
one of these?

205
00:16:19,305 --> 00:16:21,307
Oh, thank ya,
honey.

206
00:16:21,373 --> 00:16:23,250
Evelyn?

207
00:16:23,309 --> 00:16:25,482
Honey,
we gotta get goin'.

208
00:16:25,544 --> 00:16:27,956
The Braves' game's
fixin' to start...

209
00:16:28,013 --> 00:16:29,651
and you're gonna miss
your... thing.

210
00:16:29,715 --> 00:16:33,458
Excuse me.
That's my husband, Ed.

211
00:16:33,519 --> 00:16:35,590
Hi, ma'am.
How you doin'?

212
00:16:35,654 --> 00:16:39,101
Um.

213
00:16:39,158 --> 00:16:41,229
I can't believe
Buddy died.

214
00:16:41,293 --> 00:16:43,899
Neither could I.

215
00:16:43,963 --> 00:16:47,376
Oh, well, I enjoyed
talkin' to you, honey.

216
00:16:47,433 --> 00:16:49,435
What's your name?

217
00:16:49,501 --> 00:16:52,573
Evelyn...
Evelyn Couch.

218
00:16:52,638 --> 00:16:57,417
- I've got to go.
- You come back and see me,
you hear?

219
00:16:57,476 --> 00:17:01,390
- Okay.
- Bye-bye.

220
00:17:01,580 --> 00:17:03,856
First of all,
I want you...

221
00:17:03,916 --> 00:17:06,522
to truly
dedicate yourselves...

222
00:17:06,585 --> 00:17:10,624
to finding little ways
to putting that magic,
that spark...

223
00:17:10,689 --> 00:17:12,896
back into your marriage.

224
00:17:12,958 --> 00:17:16,906
When we think of
romance and marriage,

225
00:17:16,962 --> 00:17:21,001
- what is the first thought
that comes into your mind?
- Divorce!

226
00:17:21,066 --> 00:17:24,775
Remember when counselors
used to tell you to wrap
yourself in cellophane...

227
00:17:24,837 --> 00:17:27,044
to put a little charge
into your marriage?

228
00:17:27,106 --> 00:17:29,916
Do we really pay
for these lectures?

229
00:17:29,975 --> 00:17:32,683
You can see,
it is truly up to you...

230
00:17:32,745 --> 00:17:36,249
to put romance back
into your relationship.

231
00:18:03,942 --> 00:18:05,922
Evelyn,
have you gone insane?

232
00:18:05,978 --> 00:18:07,924
My God
people can see you!

233
00:18:07,980 --> 00:18:10,051
What if I had been
the paperboy?

234
00:18:10,115 --> 00:18:11,890
Get in there!

235
00:18:11,950 --> 00:18:14,760
What are you
thinking about?

236
00:18:15,554 --> 00:18:18,899
Evelyn?

237
00:18:18,957 --> 00:18:21,267
- Evelyn!
- Oh.

238
00:18:21,326 --> 00:18:25,297
You know, what we really need
instead of this baloney...

239
00:18:25,364 --> 00:18:29,437
is an assertiveness
training class for
Southern women.

240
00:18:29,501 --> 00:18:33,074
But that's a contradiction
in terms, isn't it?

241
00:18:33,138 --> 00:18:36,381
Especially you, sweetheart.
You're livin' in the Dark Ages.

242
00:18:59,631 --> 00:19:02,237
- Hi, honey.
