- Bye, Grady.

728
00:55:28,717 --> 00:55:30,162
You're gonna
get yourself in
a heap of trouble.

729
00:55:30,218 --> 00:55:34,223
What, Grady?
He's harmless.

730
00:55:34,289 --> 00:55:38,328
You shoulda seen that
big ox down by the river.

731
00:55:38,393 --> 00:55:42,432
Three solid days,
drunk as a dog,
cryin' like a baby...

732
00:55:42,497 --> 00:55:45,273
'cause Joe,
that ol' colored man
that raised him, died.

733
00:55:45,333 --> 00:55:47,279
- Remember that, Sipsey?
- Yes'm.

734
00:55:47,335 --> 00:55:50,043
- He sure ain't' jokin'
now, is he, son?
- No, ma'am.

735
00:55:50,105 --> 00:55:52,483
He won't even sit
in the same room
and have a meal today.

736
00:55:52,541 --> 00:55:57,490
Don't make no sense.
Big ox like Grady won't sit
next to a colored child,

737
00:55:57,546 --> 00:56:00,993
but he eats eggs-
Shoot right out
of a chicken's ass.

738
00:56:25,907 --> 00:56:28,581
Come on, Smokey,
let's go for a walk.

739
00:56:37,552 --> 00:56:40,328
I'm sorry about
spillin' my food, ma'am.

740
00:56:40,388 --> 00:56:44,063
I'll just
head on.

741
00:56:52,767 --> 00:56:55,805
See that piece
of land over there?

742
00:56:55,871 --> 00:56:58,681
See it?
That used to be a lake.

743
00:56:58,740 --> 00:57:00,742
Yeah.

744
00:57:00,809 --> 00:57:02,755
This one November,

745
00:57:02,811 --> 00:57:04,757
all these ducks
come by...

746
00:57:04,813 --> 00:57:08,090
and they landed
on that lake.

747
00:57:08,149 --> 00:57:12,256
Then the temperature
dropped so fast, the
whole lake just froze.

748
00:57:12,320 --> 00:57:15,358
Then the ducks
took off and took
the lake with 'em.

749
00:57:15,423 --> 00:57:18,233
Now that lake's somewhere
in Georgia, the way I hear it.

750
00:57:18,293 --> 00:57:20,967
Go on now.

751
00:57:34,576 --> 00:57:37,056
God bless you,
ma'am.

752
00:58:06,041 --> 00:58:08,317
Here, try this.

753
00:58:12,080 --> 00:58:16,119
- So what do you think?
- They're okay.

754
00:58:16,184 --> 00:58:19,893
- The truth.
- Well-

755
00:58:22,490 --> 00:58:25,266
They're terrible.

756
00:58:25,327 --> 00:58:30,276
Oh, well, don't be shy.
Tell me how you feel.

757
00:58:30,332 --> 00:58:32,869
I will.

758
00:58:45,547 --> 00:58:47,720
What'd you go
and do that for?

759
00:58:50,518 --> 00:58:53,795
I just thought you needed
a little coolin' off.

760
00:58:53,855 --> 00:58:57,962
You're right.

761
00:59:11,306 --> 00:59:14,719
Try these.

762
00:59:18,546 --> 00:59:21,220
I think we need
to make a little paste.

763
00:59:40,301 --> 00:59:43,043
What in the name
of Christmas are
you two doing?

764
00:59:43,104 --> 00:59:45,050
She's tryin'
to teach me
how to cook.

765
00:59:45,106 --> 00:59:47,985
Look at those
fried green tomatoes.

766
00:59:52,080 --> 00:59:56,426
You better stop this.
I'm gonna have to arrest you
for disorderly conduct.

767
00:59:56,484 --> 00:59:58,964
Arrest us then.
Let me handle this.

768
00:59:59,020 --> 01:00:01,296
- All right.
- Grady.

769
01:00:03,091 --> 01:00:05,594
Ha-ha-ha!

770
01:00:05,660 --> 01:00:09,836
Arrest us.
Go ahead, arrest us.

771
01:00:09,898 --> 01:00:14,278
Ruth, I have to say it.
I believe Idgie's been
a bad influence on ya.

772
01:00:14,335 --> 01:00:17,475
I agree.

773
01:00:56,478 --> 01:00:59,584
I'll be back in a minute.

774
01:00:59,647 --> 01:01:01,718
Y'all keep the show
going till then.

775
01:01:01,783 --> 01:01:03,820
We ain't goin'
nowhere.

776
01:01:04,953 --> 01:01:08,093
- ...down again.
- She's still poorly.

777
01:01:08,156 --> 01:01:11,160
Where's the baby?
Who are you?

778
01:01:12,294 --> 01:01:14,321
[Edit: Frank tries to take the baby; “a father’s right.”]

779
01:01:14,721 --> 01:01:18,760
I ain't scared
of you! No, sir!

780
01:01:18,825 --> 01:01:22,238
You should be.

781
01:01:31,972 --> 01:01:34,350
Mind your manners, boy!

782
01:01:43,249 --> 01:01:45,627
Grady,

783
01:01:45,685 --> 01:01:48,928
what does Gladys think
of you stayin' out late...

784
01:01:48,989 --> 01:01:53,301
and losin' your money to me
in poker night after night?

785
01:01:54,127 --> 01:01:56,971
She likes it
just fine.

786
01:02:01,534 --> 01:02:04,174
- They got Big George.
- Idgie!

787
01:02:04,237 --> 01:02:06,740
- Let go of him!
- Let me handle this!

788
01:02:06,806 --> 01:02:10,686
We seen how you treat
your niggers around here
and we don't like it.

789
01:02:10,744 --> 01:02:15,022
I'm the law in these parts.
I don't care what you
like or don't like.

790
01:02:15,081 --> 01:02:17,061
Turn him loose.

791
01:02:17,117 --> 01:02:20,326
Don't get riled up,
nigger lover.

792
01:02:20,387 --> 01:02:24,858
You deaf or somethin'?
I said, let him go!

793
01:02:24,924 --> 01:02:27,905
- Before you get yourselves
in a whole lot of trouble!
- Calm down.

794
01:02:27,961 --> 01:02:30,737
We wanted to have
a little get-together...

795
01:02:30,797 --> 01:02:33,778
and make sure we see
eye to eye on some things.

796
01:02:33,833 --> 01:02:37,280
You hear me now?

797
01:02:37,337 --> 01:02:39,374
Let's let him go, boys.

798
01:02:39,439 --> 01:02:41,146
We've had enough fun
for one night.

799
01:02:41,207 --> 01:02:43,153
- Turn him loose.
- Come on.

800
01:02:43,209 --> 01:02:45,189
No, you're gonna
get in trouble.

801
01:02:47,747 --> 01:02:50,284
Well, now,
that's more like it.

802
01:02:50,350 --> 01:02:53,297
Seems I don't recognize
any of you boys.

803
01:02:53,353 --> 01:02:55,594
Y'all ain't from Whistle Stop,
are you?

804
01:02:58,625 --> 01:03:00,696
This ought to do it.

805
01:03:00,760 --> 01:03:03,764
I want to thank you,
Miss Idgie.

806
01:03:03,830 --> 01:03:09,007
Forget it.
You'd have done
the same for me.

807
01:03:09,069 --> 01:03:12,881
Try to get some sleep.

808
01:03:17,677 --> 01:03:20,783
Who the hell
were those assholes?

809
01:03:20,847 --> 01:03:26,126
They's just some old boys
from Georgia come over here
to put a scare in you.

810
01:03:26,186 --> 01:03:28,632
Well, it worked.

811
01:03:28,688 --> 01:03:31,396
One of 'em was here
the other day for something,

812
01:03:31,458 --> 01:03:33,995
seen you sellin' food
to coloreds.

813
01:03:34,060 --> 01:03:38,133
They decided to come back,
shake you up a bit.

814
01:03:38,198 --> 01:03:41,645
I told 'em we don't need
anybody from Georgia
comin' over here...

815
01:03:41,701 --> 01:03:44,238
tellin' us what
we can or cannot do.

816
01:03:44,304 --> 01:03:49,481
They won't be back.
I guaran-gol-damn-tee
you that.

817
01:03:49,542 --> 01:03:52,614
One other thing,
little Miss Smarty-pants,

818
01:03:52,679 --> 01:03:56,957
I do not wear a size 14 shoe...

819
01:03:57,016 --> 01:04:00,589
and I don't
much care for parades,

820
01:04:00,653 --> 01:04:04,260
bedsheets or otherwise.

821
01:04:18,897 --> 01:04:22,397
[Edit: “It was Frank. He saw the baby.” / Klan aftermath]

822
01:04:48,827 --> 01:04:52,172
- Hey there!
- You got to come quick.

823
01:04:52,230 --> 01:04:55,404
Well, the show
has hardly begun.

824
01:04:55,467 --> 01:04:58,209
You got to come quick now.
You hear me?

825
01:05:00,939 --> 01:05:03,249
- Run, get help!
Run, quick!
- Where's the baby?

826
01:05:03,308 --> 01:05:05,345
Never mind.

827
01:05:24,762 --> 01:05:30,303
Excuse me, sir.
I don't believe you
should be goin' anywhere...

828
01:05:30,368 --> 01:05:32,939
with Ruth's baby.

829
01:06:16,640 --> 01:06:18,140
[Edit: Sheriff Curtis Smoote looking for a fella (Frank investigation)]

830
01:06:18,140 --> 01:06:19,285
What's he done?

831
01:06:19,350 --> 01:06:23,355
Nothin' that we know of.
We're tryin' to find out
what's been did to him.

832
01:06:23,420 --> 01:06:26,924
He told his hired man he was
comin' to see his wife and baby,

833
01:06:26,991 --> 01:06:30,996
but he ain't never
showed up back home.

834
01:06:31,061 --> 01:06:33,769
Hell, I told him
if he showed up in this town,

835
01:06:33,831 --> 01:06:35,970
we'd all have known.

836
01:06:36,033 --> 01:06:38,479
Looks a little sissified
to me.

837
01:06:38,536 --> 01:06:42,541
From what I hear,
most you boys in Georgia...

838
01:06:42,606 --> 01:06:44,051
are a little light
on your feet

839
01:06:44,108 --> 01:06:47,282
That's the way
I heard it.

840
01:06:47,344 --> 01:06:49,483
Could I interest you
in some pie?

841
01:06:49,547 --> 01:06:53,461
No, ma'am, but that
barbecue sure smells good.

842
01:06:53,517 --> 01:06:56,964
Best damn barbecue
in the state of Alabama.

843
01:07:26,183 --> 01:07:28,823
Here you go.
That's your 4th one today.

844
01:07:28,886 --> 01:07:31,730
I swear you're about
to eat up all my barbecue.

845
01:07:31,789 --> 01:07:34,565
Sit down.

846
01:07:34,625 --> 01:07:37,606
Sit down.

847
01:07:39,139 --> 01:07:42,639
[Edit: Smoote: hired hand said Idgie threatened to kill Frank]

848
01:07:45,236 --> 01:07:47,910
You sure you ain't
never seen this man, boy?

849
01:07:47,972 --> 01:07:51,613
Yes, sir, and I already told ya,
I ain't never seen him.

850
01:07:51,676 --> 01:07:54,179
You'd do anything for
Miss Idgie, wouldn't ya, boy?

851
01:07:56,080 --> 01:07:58,026
Yes, sir.

852
01:08:01,252 --> 01:08:04,859
Would ya kill for her?
Did ya kill for her?

853
01:08:12,230 --> 01:08:14,369
No, sir.

854
01:08:14,432 --> 01:08:19,279
Well, now, maybe
one of these days
you'll tell the truth.

855
01:08:21,306 --> 01:08:24,014
Just remember, we hang
lyin' niggers in Georgia...

856
01:08:24,075 --> 01:08:27,056
just as fast as
they do in Alabama.

857
01:08:27,111 --> 01:08:30,888
Yes, sir, I remember.

858
01:09:08,453 --> 01:09:12,902
Sorry.

859
01:09:12,957 --> 01:09:17,906
- What are ya
doin' in here?
- No milk in the house.

860
01:09:17,962 --> 01:09:20,067
Where were you?

861
01:09:20,131 --> 01:09:23,078
Takin' care of business,
havin' a good time.

862
01:09:25,803 --> 01:09:29,376
I've been thinkin'
maybe I should move on...

863
01:09:29,416 --> 01:09:30,916
[Edit: Idgie/Ruth after Frank]

864
01:09:32,251 --> 01:09:34,197
You don't believe me.

865
01:09:34,253 --> 01:09:38,827
Right now, I don't know
what to believe.

866
01:09:41,293 --> 01:09:44,604
Believe me when I tell ya
I don't want ya to move out.

867
01:10:10,189 --> 01:10:13,534
Finally.

868
01:10:13,592 --> 01:10:17,335
Thanks, I've been
out here all day.

869
01:10:44,490 --> 01:10:46,902
Excuse me.
I was waiting for that space.

870
01:10:46,959 --> 01:10:51,908
- Yeah? Tough!
- Face it, lady,
we're younger and faster.

871
01:11:12,451 --> 01:11:15,364
Towanda.

872
01:11:18,858 --> 01:11:21,896
Ha-ha-ha-ha!

873
01:11:21,961 --> 01:11:26,876
Yeah!
Whooo!

874
01:11:31,237 --> 01:11:33,717
Towanda!

875
01:11:38,577 --> 01:11:41,387
Yes, ma'am.

876
01:11:41,447 --> 01:11:44,155
Whoooo!

877
01:11:47,152 --> 01:11:50,656
- Help, someone!
- What are you doing?
Are you crazy?

878
01:11:50,723 --> 01:11:55,672
Face it, girls.
I'm older, and I
have more insurance.

879
01:12:04,270 --> 01:12:07,911
I never get mad,
Mrs. Threadgoode.
Never!

880
01:12:07,973 --> 01:12:10,544
The way I was raised
it was bad manners.

881
01:12:10,609 --> 01:12:13,783
Well, I got mad
and it felt terrific.

882
01:12:13,846 --> 01:12:17,157
I felt like I could beat
the shit outta all those punks!

883
01:12:17,216 --> 01:12:19,958
Excuse my language.
just beat 'em to a pulp!

884
01:12:20,019 --> 01:12:22,158
Beat 'em till
they begged for mercy.

885
01:12:22,221 --> 01:12:24,258
Towanda, the avenger!

886
01:12:26,176 --> 01:12:27,676
[Edit: Towanda rant naming wife-beaters like Frank Bennett]

887
01:12:27,676 --> 01:12:29,965
I'll give half the military
budget to people over 65...

888
01:12:30,029 --> 01:12:32,771
and declare wrinkles
sexually desirable.

889
01:12:32,832 --> 01:12:37,474
Towanda, righter of wrongs,
queen beyond compare!

890
01:12:37,536 --> 01:12:40,847
How many of them
hormones you takin', honey?

891
01:12:56,322 --> 01:12:58,825
what I can't
understand is...

892
01:12:58,891 --> 01:13:02,498
how in the hell
you can hit someone...

893
01:13:02,561 --> 01:13:04,802
six times
by accident.

894
01:13:04,864 --> 01:13:07,902
Oh, Ed, don't make
such a big deal about it.

895
01:13:14,306 --> 01:13:18,846
- What the hell is this?
- A low cholesterol meal.

896
01:13:18,911 --> 01:13:20,857
Happy Valentine's.

897
01:13:24,116 --> 01:13:27,063
My God!
Are you tryin' to kill me?

898
01:13:27,119 --> 01:13:30,396
If I was gonna kill ya,
I'd use my hands.

899
01:13:47,306 --> 01:13:49,912
I'm worried about
my little friend Evelyn.

900
01:13:49,975 --> 01:13:52,546
She said her husband...

901
01:13:52,611 --> 01:13:54,921
will just be watching
his sports on TV...

902
01:13:54,980 --> 01:13:58,154
and she has an urge to hit him
in the head with a baseball bat.

903
01:13:58,217 --> 01:14:01,096
Hell, that
seems normal to me.

904
01:14:01,153 --> 01:14:03,155
- Hi Janeen.
- Mm-hmm

905
01:14:03,222 --> 01:14:05,702
Mrs. Threadgoode, would
you like some crudites?

906
01:14:07,111 --> 01:14:10,611
[Edit: Evelyn asks if Idgie murdered Frank]

907
01:14:14,708 --> 01:14:16,654
Buddy.

908
01:14:16,710 --> 01:14:18,656
Everybody
outta the way.

909
01:14:18,712 --> 01:14:22,489
Give him here.
Let him go. I've got him.

910
01:14:24,452 --> 01:14:26,659
Come on. You're
gonna be all right.

911
01:14:26,720 --> 01:14:29,064
Open the door!

912
01:14:29,123 --> 01:14:33,196
Put him in the car.
It's all right, honey

913
01:14:54,415 --> 01:14:56,326
I can understand...

914
01:14:56,383 --> 01:14:58,920
having a funeral
for an arm.

915
01:14:58,986 --> 01:15:02,524
I just don't know why
she insists on callin'
him "Stump."?

916
01:15:02,590 --> 01:15:05,594
She say everybody else gonna
be callin' him that...

917
01:15:05,659 --> 01:15:09,766
so we might just as well
be the first.

918
01:15:09,830 --> 01:15:14,006
Okay, ice cream
and cake for everybody.

919
01:15:14,068 --> 01:15:15,877
Go on.

920
01:15:20,141 --> 01:15:24,146
My daddy always used to say
there was a separate God
for children.

921
01:15:28,015 --> 01:15:31,553
The good Lord was watchin'
over stump that day.

922
01:15:31,619 --> 01:15:34,998
But then it started to rain
that month.

923
01:15:36,116 --> 01:15:37,616
[Edit: Flood / Frank’s pickup found; Idgie in trouble]

924
01:15:37,616 --> 01:15:39,844
When her husband came back
to get her and take her home,

925
01:15:39,910 --> 01:15:44,552
you and your colored man
murdered him in cold blood.

926
01:15:45,749 --> 01:15:47,353
No, sir.

927
01:15:47,417 --> 01:15:52,696
Well, where were you on the
night of September 30, 1933?

928
01:15:52,756 --> 01:15:55,066
I was at the town hall
doing a show.

929
01:15:55,125 --> 01:15:58,231
- And after that?
- I was at
my mother's house.

930
01:15:58,295 --> 01:16:00,832
Oh, yeah?
Who was with you?

931
01:16:00,897 --> 01:16:05,243
- Just Big George and myself
- What about your mother?
Can she confirm that?

932
01:16:05,302 --> 01:16:07,578
No, sir.
She died a year ago.

933
01:16:07,637 --> 01:16:10,140
I'm sorry to hear that.

934
01:16:10,207 --> 01:16:13,916
But do you expect 12 intelligent
men to believe you,

935
01:16:13,977 --> 01:16:16,617
although one witness is dead and
the other is a colored man,

936
01:16:16,680 --> 01:16:20,093
known to be a worthless,
no-good, lying nigger?

937
01:16:20,150 --> 01:16:22,426
You expect these men
to take your word for it...

938
01:16:22,486 --> 01:16:25,160
just because
you say so?

939
01:16:25,222 --> 01:16:29,762
That's right,
you gump-faced, blown-up,
baboon-assed bastard!

940
01:16:29,826 --> 01:16:33,296
One more outburst
like that...

941
01:16:33,363 --> 01:16:36,867
and I'll hold you
in contempt of court.
You understand?

942
01:16:36,933 --> 01:16:39,743
Yes, sir.

943
01:16:41,438 --> 01:16:45,011
- Oh, Lord.
- Next witness.

944
01:16:47,577 --> 01:16:49,056
Did you know that
you were pregnant'...

945
01:16:49,456 --> 01:16:52,956
[Edit: Trial: Ruth left Frank willingly; would not raise her child with him]

946
01:16:53,359 --> 01:16:56,966
of Idgie Threadgoode
and her colored man,
known as Big George,

947
01:16:57,029 --> 01:17:00,806
on the night
of September 30, 1933?

948
01:17:00,866 --> 01:17:02,846
Yes, sir,
I do.

949
01:17:02,902 --> 01:17:05,348
It has been
suggested here...

950
01:17:05,404 --> 01:17:08,874
that she and her colored man
were at her mother's house.

951
01:17:08,941 --> 01:17:13,185
- Can you confirm that?
- No, sir.
That is a lie.

952
01:17:13,245 --> 01:17:15,987
Oh, shit.

953
01:17:16,048 --> 01:17:19,291
It has been my habit
to write all the dates...

954
01:17:19,351 --> 01:17:22,298
Of the activities of
the church in my Bible.

955
01:17:22,354 --> 01:17:27,030
I show that the night
of September 30, 1933...

956
01:17:27,092 --> 01:17:30,130
was the start of our
annual revival...

957
01:17:30,195 --> 01:17:32,971
down at the
Baptist campground.

958
01:17:33,032 --> 01:17:35,137
Sister Threadgoode
was there...

959
01:17:35,200 --> 01:17:39,239
along with her hired man,
George Pullman,

960
01:17:39,305 --> 01:17:43,447
who was in charge of the
barbecue as he has been...

961
01:17:43,509 --> 01:17:46,183
- for the last ten years.
- Objection.

962
01:17:46,245 --> 01:17:50,785
That doesn't mean anything.
Murder could've taken place any
time the next couple of clays.

963
01:17:50,849 --> 01:17:55,889
- Have you ever been to one
of our revivals, sir?
- Well, no.

964
01:17:55,955 --> 01:17:58,026
Do you attend church
regularly, sir?

965
01:17:58,090 --> 01:18:00,297
'Course I do.

966
01:18:00,359 --> 01:18:04,899
Good. Well, maybe if you
attended one of our revivals,

967
01:18:04,964 --> 01:18:07,342
you'd know
they last three days...

968
01:18:07,399 --> 01:18:09,743
and three nights,
Your Honor.

969
01:18:12,004 --> 01:18:14,985
Approach the bench.

970
01:18:15,040 --> 01:18:19,750
Percy, it don't look like
you got a case at all.

971
01:18:19,812 --> 01:18:22,383
In the first place,
there's no body.

972
01:18:22,448 --> 01:18:25,725
Second, we got us a preacher
nobody's gonna dispute.

973
01:18:26,495 --> 01:18:29,995
[Edit: Judge: Frank got drunk, drove into the river; case dismissed]

974
01:18:34,843 --> 01:18:37,756
See you in church,
Sister?

975
01:18:38,647 --> 01:18:40,888
Reverend.

976
01:18:40,949 --> 01:18:45,261
I can't believe he
actually swore on a Bible.

977
01:18:45,320 --> 01:18:47,266
Well, not really.

978
01:18:47,322 --> 01:18:49,324
If that judge
had looked closer,

979
01:18:49,391 --> 01:18:52,463
he'd have seen it was really
a copy of Moby Dick.

980
01:18:54,496 --> 01:18:58,911
- But why did he do it?
- For the sheer joy of
seeing you in church again...

981
01:18:58,967 --> 01:19:01,811
which I suggested to him
might be your penance.

982
01:19:01,870 --> 01:19:04,510
- You didn't promise him,
did you?
- Yes, ma'am, I did.

983
01:19:04,573 --> 01:19:06,519
And I never
break my word.

984
01:19:06,575 --> 01:19:10,955
If I live 1,000 years,
I will never forgive you.

985
01:19:11,013 --> 01:19:15,189
I don't know what's worse,
church or jail.

986
01:19:26,161 --> 01:19:29,301
There now.
Don't you look pretty?

987
01:19:29,364 --> 01:19:31,503
Oh, yes, honey.

988
01:19:31,567 --> 01:19:36,243
You'll have me
lookin' like Ginger Rogers
before you're done.

989
01:19:36,305 --> 01:19:40,549
Don't let Mr. Dunaway see me.
He's liable to go wild.

990
01:19:42,044 --> 01:19:45,287
I'm glad to see
you're in a good mood.

991
01:19:45,347 --> 01:19:48,487
You've slimmed down quite a bit
in the last few weeks.

992
01:19:48,550 --> 01:19:52,862
I'm just so happy Big George
and Idgie got off.

993
01:19:53,457 --> 01:19:56,957
[Edit: “I would have killed Frank Bennett if I could’ve” / dead men tell no tales]

994
01:19:57,107 --> 01:19:59,507
Frank Bennett on-screen scenes removed

995
01:20:15,644 --> 01:20:18,682
Evelyn, what in the hell
are you doing?

996
01:20:18,747 --> 01:20:21,660
I need some light
and air.

997
01:20:21,716 --> 01:20:24,925
Why don't you take
one of your walks
or your jog...

998
01:20:24,986 --> 01:20:28,524
or whatever it is
you do?

999
01:20:28,590 --> 01:20:31,503
There's no dinner
either!

1000
01:20:31,559 --> 01:20:36,008
Ed, you have any idea
why I've been goin'
to all these classes?

1001
01:20:36,064 --> 01:20:39,602
- No.
- I've been trying to save
our marriage.

1002
01:20:39,668 --> 01:20:41,705
What's the point
of my tryin'...

1003
01:20:41,770 --> 01:20:46,446
if you're gonna sit on
your butt drinking beer...

1004
01:20:46,508 --> 01:20:49,352
and watching baseball,
basketball, football...

1005
01:20:49,411 --> 01:20:52,551
bowling and hockey
and golf...

1006
01:20:52,614 --> 01:20:56,494
and Challenge
of the Gladiators?

1007
01:21:02,190 --> 01:21:06,730
Mrs. Couch, I'm Sue,
Mrs. Otis' daughter-in-law.

1008
01:21:06,795 --> 01:21:10,242
How are you?
I've heard about you
from Mrs. Threadgoode.

1009
01:21:10,298 --> 01:21:14,007
She is so sweet. She's been
lookin' after my mother-in-law.

1010
01:21:14,069 --> 01:21:16,845
Now, how is
Mrs. Otis doin',
by the way?

1011
01:21:16,905 --> 01:21:21,376
Much better, thank you.
It takes time getting used
to a strange place.

1012
01:21:21,443 --> 01:21:25,482
I'm glad to hear it.
Mrs. Threadgoode's
been anxious to get home.

1013
01:21:25,547 --> 01:21:29,757
Mrs. Couch, Mrs. Threadgoode
doesn't have a house anymore.

1014
01:21:29,818 --> 01:21:33,288
- They tore
that down.
- What?

1015
01:21:33,354 --> 01:21:37,598
They had to.
It was falling apart,
and it was condemned.

1016
01:21:37,659 --> 01:21:40,606
Oh, no.

1017
01:21:40,662 --> 01:21:44,872
- Does she know that?
- No, well, we didn't see
any point in telling her.

1018
01:21:44,933 --> 01:21:47,436
It would just break her heart,
poor old thing

1019
01:21:47,502 --> 01:21:51,450
But I am so glad
I got a chance to meet you.

1020
01:21:51,506 --> 01:21:54,715
You take care of yourself now.
Bye-bye.

1021
01:23:04,679 --> 01:23:06,989
Oh, Evelyn. hey!

1022
01:23:07,048 --> 01:23:09,528
Hey-

1023
01:23:09,584 --> 01:23:11,962
Do you like
my roses?

1024
01:23:12,020 --> 01:23:15,365
Since I can't get home
to look at my own roses...

1025
01:23:15,423 --> 01:23:17,801
I made myself
a paper garden.

1026
01:23:17,859 --> 01:23:21,363
- Got everything
but the bugs.
- They're lovely.

1027
01:23:21,429 --> 01:23:24,706
- You been here long?
- Happy birthday!

1028
01:23:24,766 --> 01:23:27,269
- Oh!
- I shouldn't
have woken you up.

1029
01:23:27,335 --> 01:23:31,613
'Course you should've.
Don't you never let me sleep
through a visitor's day, honey.

1030
01:23:31,673 --> 01:23:36,418
- I look forward to them all week.
- So do I, Mrs. Threadgoode.

1031
01:23:36,477 --> 01:23:39,822
Oh! I can't believe
you remembered.

1032
01:23:39,881 --> 01:23:44,091
You made me
fried green tomatoes!

1033
01:23:46,521 --> 01:23:48,558
Mmm!
They're delicious.

1034
01:23:48,623 --> 01:23:51,968
- It's your recipe.
Are they cold?
- No.
They're just the way...

1035
01:23:52,026 --> 01:23:56,304
- we used to have 'em
at the Whistle Stop Cafe.
- Mmm!

1036
01:23:56,364 --> 01:24:00,312
You couldn't be sweeter to me
if you was my own daughter.

1037
01:24:00,368 --> 01:24:02,541
Here's your napkin.

1038
01:24:02,604 --> 01:24:04,641
And wait-wait-wait.

1039
01:24:04,706 --> 01:24:07,277
Queen, queen.

1040
01:24:10,445 --> 01:24:14,587
You know,
I don't feel 83.

1041
01:24:14,649 --> 01:24:18,791
It sorta slipped up on me.

1042
01:24:20,889 --> 01:24:24,336
I never expected
to live this long.

1043
01:24:24,392 --> 01:24:30,001
'Course, the Lord takes us home
when he wants us.

1044
01:24:39,007 --> 01:24:42,648
Are you all right?

1045
01:24:42,710 --> 01:24:45,054
I was thinking
about Ruth.

1046
01:24:45,113 --> 01:24:47,923
After the trial
was over,

1047
01:24:47,982 --> 01:24:50,189
Everything went back
to normal...

1048
01:24:50,251 --> 01:24:54,028
till that fall
when Ruth lost her appetite.

1049
01:24:54,088 --> 01:24:56,659
By the time Doc Hadley
looked at her,

1050
01:24:56,724 --> 01:25:00,934
he said the cancer was so bad
she only had a couple of weeks.

1051
01:25:00,995 --> 01:25:03,737
Well, we moved her
to the Threadgoode house...

1052
01:25:03,798 --> 01:25:08,645
and put her downstairs
so she'd be more comfortable.

1053
01:25:08,703 --> 01:25:13,209
Sipsey moved in with her
and never left her side.

1054
01:25:13,274 --> 01:25:15,413
Hold on, baby
I'm right here.

1055
01:25:15,476 --> 01:25:20,152
Idgie just prayed
for a miracle.

1056
01:25:39,434 --> 01:25:42,904
Now, listen to me.

1057
01:25:42,971 --> 01:25:45,508
Make sure he graduates.

1058
01:25:45,573 --> 01:25:49,783
And don't... let him
come to the funeral.

1059
01:25:49,844 --> 01:25:52,518
I don't want him going
through that mess.

1060
01:25:52,580 --> 01:25:55,891
Would you quit talkin'
like that?

1061
01:25:55,950 --> 01:25:58,453
What funeral?

1062
01:25:58,519 --> 01:26:00,897
You're gonna be back on
your feet feelin' just fine...

1063
01:26:00,955 --> 01:26:03,629
in just a few days.

1064
01:26:03,691 --> 01:26:06,604
Just you wait.

1065
01:26:06,661 --> 01:26:09,801
Oh, what's the matter,
son?

1066
01:26:15,636 --> 01:26:19,311
Well,
let's go for a walk.

1067
01:26:20,008 --> 01:26:21,612
Did you get
into a fight?

1068
01:26:21,676 --> 01:26:24,384
I got punched
in the nose.

1069
01:26:24,445 --> 01:26:27,949
I can't play
like everyone else.

1070
01:26:28,016 --> 01:26:31,554
Did I ever tell you the
story about... the oysters?

1071
01:26:31,619 --> 01:26:34,099
All the millions of 'em
just lying around-

1072
01:26:34,155 --> 01:26:39,002
- And God put sand in one of 'em,
and it makes a pearl.
- Oh.

1073
01:26:40,762 --> 01:26:43,436
Did I ever tell you about
Eva's three-legged dog?

1074
01:26:43,498 --> 01:26:45,603
How it never felt sorry
for itself...

1075
01:26:45,666 --> 01:26:49,307
and howl ought to be
smarter than a dumb dog
and not feel sorry for myself.

1076
01:26:51,105 --> 01:26:54,450
You listen to everything
I say, don't you?

1077
01:26:54,509 --> 01:26:57,490
You get real mad at me
when I don't.

1078
01:26:57,545 --> 01:26:59,252
Well,

1079
01:27:01,716 --> 01:27:04,720
you know about
your mama.

1080
01:27:04,786 --> 01:27:07,289
She's sick.

1081
01:27:07,355 --> 01:27:09,392
Mm-hmm.

1082
01:27:10,925 --> 01:27:14,372
See, now is the time
for courage.

1083
01:27:14,429 --> 01:27:18,138
I guess you already know
that there are...

1084
01:27:18,199 --> 01:27:21,203
angels masqueradin' as people
walkin' around this planet,

1085
01:27:21,269 --> 01:27:24,443
and your mom's
the bravest one of those.

1086
01:27:28,709 --> 01:27:30,814
Come here.

1087
01:27:38,519 --> 01:27:40,931
Mama, I can hit!
You should see me.

1088
01:27:40,988 --> 01:27:43,798
Idgie, she hit me in
the back with a curveball.

1089
01:27:43,858 --> 01:27:46,031
I didn't duck,
and I hardly cried.

1090
01:27:46,094 --> 01:27:49,564
She hit you?

1091
01:27:49,630 --> 01:27:53,635
Well, she did that
to me once too,

1092
01:27:53,701 --> 01:27:56,477
but I think
I did cry.

1093
01:27:58,372 --> 01:28:02,343
Mama, I'm sorry
if you're sad.

1094
01:28:02,410 --> 01:28:04,720
Well,

1095
01:28:04,779 --> 01:28:07,885
give me a big kiss then,
and I'll never be sad again.

1096
01:28:15,423 --> 01:28:18,336
And you best not be sad
neither.

1097
01:28:18,392 --> 01:28:21,635
You understand?

1098
01:28:21,696 --> 01:28:23,642
You promise?

1099
01:28:23,698 --> 01:28:25,735
Promise.

1100
01:28:25,800 --> 01:28:29,748
Attaboy.
You go and wash up.

1101
01:28:53,561 --> 01:28:55,598
Sweet baby.

1102
01:28:59,567 --> 01:29:02,844
You two
be alone now.

1103
01:29:03,538 --> 01:29:07,213
Hey, girl.

1104
01:29:09,710 --> 01:29:11,781
No.

1105
01:29:13,714 --> 01:29:16,786
That's nice.

1106
01:29:17,785 --> 01:29:21,494
Will you do one thing
for me?

1107
01:29:21,556 --> 01:29:25,163
- Yeah, anything.
- Be good to yourself.

1108
01:29:25,226 --> 01:29:28,173
Even...

1109
01:29:28,229 --> 01:29:30,766
settle down if
you can find someone...

1110
01:29:30,831 --> 01:29:33,573
who can beat you
in poker.

1111
01:29:41,275 --> 01:29:46,247
There's so many things
I want to say to you.

1112
01:29:46,314 --> 01:29:48,851
No.

1113
01:29:49,684 --> 01:29:52,358
I love your stories.

1114
01:29:52,420 --> 01:29:55,367
Tell me a story,
Idgie.

1115
01:29:58,226 --> 01:30:02,072
Oh, God.

1116
01:30:02,129 --> 01:30:05,235
Go on,
you old' bee charmer.

1117
01:30:05,299 --> 01:30:08,974
Tell me
a good tall tale.

1118
01:30:10,371 --> 01:30:14,080
Tell me the one
about the lake.

1119
01:30:15,376 --> 01:30:20,018
- What lake?
- The one...
that used to be here.

1120
01:30:22,149 --> 01:30:24,095
Oh.

1121
01:30:26,153 --> 01:30:29,726
Well, that was
just a lie.

1122
01:30:29,790 --> 01:30:32,566
I know that, fool.

1123
01:30:32,627 --> 01:30:34,698
Tell me anyway.

1124
01:30:34,762 --> 01:30:38,175
Tell me the story.

1125
01:30:39,734 --> 01:30:43,181
Well...

1126
01:30:45,206 --> 01:30:47,686
one time...

1127
01:30:47,742 --> 01:30:50,552
there was this lake.

1128
01:30:54,982 --> 01:30:59,362
And, uh, it was
right outside of town.

1129
01:30:59,420 --> 01:31:04,870
We used to go
fishin' and swimmin'
and canoein' in it.

1130
01:31:04,925 --> 01:31:08,168
And see,
one November...

1131
01:31:08,229 --> 01:31:10,539
this big ﬂock
of ducks...

1132
01:31:10,598 --> 01:31:15,638
came in and landed
on that lake and, uh,

1133
01:31:15,703 --> 01:31:20,550
and then the temperature
dropped so fast that the
lake just froze right there.

1134
01:31:20,608 --> 01:31:22,884
And the, uh,

1135
01:31:22,943 --> 01:31:26,720
the ducks, they...

1136
01:31:26,781 --> 01:31:30,957
ﬂew off, you see,
and took that lake with 'em.

1137
01:31:31,018 --> 01:31:34,261
And, uh.

1138
01:31:34,322 --> 01:31:39,328
Now they say that lake is
somewhere over in Georgia.

1139
01:31:39,393 --> 01:31:42,465
Can you imagine?

1140
01:32:40,154 --> 01:32:43,431
It's all right,
honey.

1141
01:32:43,491 --> 01:32:46,028
Let her go.

1142
01:32:46,093 --> 01:32:49,472
Let her go.

1143
01:32:49,530 --> 01:32:53,774
You know,
Miss Ruth was a lady.

1144
01:32:53,834 --> 01:32:57,111
And a lady
always knows...

1145
01:32:57,171 --> 01:33:00,175
when to leave.

1146
01:33:05,679 --> 01:33:09,786
When I think on our
departed sister, Ruth Jamison,

1147
01:33:09,850 --> 01:33:12,956
I'm reminded of our
Lord's Sermon on the Mount...

1148
01:33:13,020 --> 01:33:15,500
and how his teachings-

1149
01:33:15,556 --> 01:33:20,005
It's funny how strong
Ruth affected everyone.

1150
01:33:20,060 --> 01:33:23,473
even Smokey Lonesome.

1151
01:33:23,531 --> 01:33:26,205
When he died
a few years back...

1152
01:33:26,267 --> 01:33:28,975
he had one possession
on him,

1153
01:33:29,036 --> 01:33:31,642
A picture of Ruth.

1154
01:33:33,007 --> 01:33:37,114
He was in love with her
from the first time he saw her.

1155
01:33:37,178 --> 01:33:40,057
We all were.

1156
01:33:46,020 --> 01:33:48,500
I shouldn't
a-told you this.

1157
01:33:50,424 --> 01:33:54,395
I hate death.
It scares me so.

1158
01:33:54,462 --> 01:33:56,999
Death is nothin'
to be afraid of!

1159
01:33:57,064 --> 01:34:00,136
Look at me. I'm at
the jumpin'-off place,

1160
01:34:00,201 --> 01:34:03,444
and I ain't afraid
one bit.

1161
01:34:03,504 --> 01:34:07,213
Oh, Ninny,
you're so brave.

1162
01:34:08,776 --> 01:34:12,724
Ruth and Idgie were brave,
not me.

1163
01:34:12,780 --> 01:34:16,159
I wouldn't be afraid
of death if I was you.

1164
01:34:16,217 --> 01:34:21,166
I'd be more afraid of driving
in rush-hour traffic.

1165
01:36:16,370 --> 01:36:19,374
Hi, honey.
Look what I got you.

1166
01:36:19,440 --> 01:36:21,477
Ah...

1167
01:36:21,542 --> 01:36:25,012
Ed, how sweet!

1168
01:36:25,079 --> 01:36:27,525
- Lilies!
My favorite.
- Yeah.

1169
01:36:27,581 --> 01:36:30,721
I know.
Sometimes I even amaze myself.

1170
01:36:30,784 --> 01:36:34,891
- What's the occasion?
- Oh, honey,
I just...

1171
01:36:34,955 --> 01:36:37,936
feel sorry about
the past few months.

1172
01:36:37,992 --> 01:36:41,997
I don't know what
you're really up to and
what's going on with you,

1173
01:36:42,062 --> 01:36:46,477
but I guess I could've been
more helpful with your job
and everything, you know.

1174
01:36:47,701 --> 01:36:49,578
Well, why are you...

1175
01:36:49,637 --> 01:36:52,618
puttin' up this wall
where you just tore one down?

1176
01:36:52,673 --> 01:36:55,813
Well...
I changed my mind.

1177
01:36:55,876 --> 01:36:58,652
I don't mean to seem
dense or anything,

1178
01:36:58,712 --> 01:37:02,956
- but what's changed?
- The air and the light.

1179
01:37:05,319 --> 01:37:07,925
- Ed-
- Hmm?

1180
01:37:07,988 --> 01:37:10,468
You remember how
you used to tell me...

1181
01:37:10,524 --> 01:37:13,266
you always wanted
two women in your house?

1182
01:37:13,327 --> 01:37:15,637
Oh, God.

1183
01:37:15,696 --> 01:37:17,369
Yeah.

1184
01:37:17,431 --> 01:37:19,468
Well...

1185
01:37:19,533 --> 01:37:22,480
what if I was
the younger of the two?

1186
01:37:22,536 --> 01:37:26,074
I don't believe
I get your drift.

1187
01:37:26,140 --> 01:37:30,680
I want something
more than I've ever
wanted anything before.

1188
01:37:30,744 --> 01:37:33,520
I want to bring
Mrs. Threadgoode...

1189
01:37:33,580 --> 01:37:35,787
to our home.

1190
01:37:35,849 --> 01:37:38,489
I want her
to live here with us.

1191
01:37:38,552 --> 01:37:41,055
I want to give her the love
she's given me.

1192
01:37:41,121 --> 01:37:45,297
You're kiddin' me, aren't you?
I'm absolutely serious.

1193
01:37:45,359 --> 01:37:50,206
That's why I'm puttin' the
wall to Kyle's room back up.

1194
01:37:50,264 --> 01:37:53,336
Well, honey, this isn't
something you're just go and do.

1195
01:37:53,400 --> 01:37:56,074
I mean,
she's an old woman.

1196
01:37:56,136 --> 01:37:59,379
What if she got sick?
Who's gonna take care of her?

1197
01:37:59,440 --> 01:38:01,147
I will!

1198
01:38:01,208 --> 01:38:03,210
I can't leave her
in that place.

1199
01:38:03,277 --> 01:38:07,191
She's not a stray cat.
Hell, she isn't even family.

1200
01:38:07,247 --> 01:38:10,319
- She's family to me.
- Now, Evelyn.

1201
01:38:11,151 --> 01:38:14,223
Evelyn?

1202
01:38:14,288 --> 01:38:16,165
Honey?

1203
01:38:16,223 --> 01:38:18,225
Ah, look...

1204
01:38:18,292 --> 01:38:22,536
have you mentioned this
harebrained idea to her?

1205
01:38:22,596 --> 01:38:25,668
- Not yet.
- Well, good!

1206
01:38:25,733 --> 01:38:28,213
Then we'll just pretend
it never happened.

1207
01:38:28,268 --> 01:38:31,306
I'm making my own money.
I'll pay for everything.

1208
01:38:31,371 --> 01:38:34,944
You don't have to do
a thing.

1209
01:38:35,008 --> 01:38:37,511
Evelyn...

1210
01:38:37,578 --> 01:38:40,058
it's never
gonna happen.

1211
01:38:40,114 --> 01:38:42,788
So just forget
about it.

1212
01:38:44,384 --> 01:38:47,160
Don't you ever
say "never" to me.

1213
01:38:56,096 --> 01:38:58,906
Someone helped put a mirror
up in front of my face,

1214
01:38:58,966 --> 01:39:01,572
and I didn't like
what I saw one bit.

1215
01:39:01,635 --> 01:39:05,481
You know what I did?
I changed.

1216
01:39:05,539 --> 01:39:09,453
And that someone...
was Mrs. Threadgoode.

1217
01:39:09,510 --> 01:39:14,016
She needs my love
and care, and I'm
gonna give it to her.

1218
01:39:15,783 --> 01:39:19,424
If you'll excuse me,
I have to go to the gym.

1219
01:39:24,358 --> 01:39:27,396
And if you won't listen
to reason...

1220
01:39:27,461 --> 01:39:31,102
there's always Towanda.

1221
01:39:45,879 --> 01:39:48,860
Hey, Nin-

1222
01:39:51,518 --> 01:39:54,556
What are you doing?

1223
01:39:54,621 --> 01:39:57,363
Those are her things,
Mrs. Threadgoode's things!

1224
01:39:57,424 --> 01:40:00,530
- What are you doing in here?
Where's Mrs. Threadgoode?
- Who?

1225
01:40:00,594 --> 01:40:03,438
Mrs. Threadgoode!
The woman who lives here.
Are you deaf?

1226
01:40:03,497 --> 01:40:06,410
I'm sorry, miss.
All they told me...

1227
01:40:06,466 --> 01:40:10,676
was that the woman who lived
in here died this morning.

1228
01:40:12,539 --> 01:40:14,678
Oh. my God!

1229
01:40:14,741 --> 01:40:19,087
Wha- What
are you sayin'?

1230
01:40:19,146 --> 01:40:21,319
She died early
this morning.

1231
01:40:21,381 --> 01:40:25,727
They were shorthanded
so they asked me to take
all this stuff down.

1232
01:40:25,786 --> 01:40:28,289
That? all I know.

1233
01:40:47,674 --> 01:40:49,620
Stop that!

1234
01:40:49,676 --> 01:40:52,054
What is the matter
with you people?

1235
01:40:52,112 --> 01:40:55,059
Can't you wait a goddamn day,
for Chrissake?

1236
01:40:55,115 --> 01:40:58,119
Do you have no respect?
These are her things!

1237
01:40:58,185 --> 01:41:02,361
I'm sorry, but they told me
to get this room ready
for another patient.

1238
01:41:02,422 --> 01:41:05,631
She may be just
another patient to you,

1239
01:41:05,692 --> 01:41:09,799
- but she was my friend,
and I loved her.
- I'm sorry.

1240
01:41:09,863 --> 01:41:11,809
I'm just
following orders.

1241
01:41:11,865 --> 01:41:14,812
- What is going on?
- Why didn't
you call me?

1242
01:41:14,868 --> 01:41:18,213
- You could've called me before
you sent that idiot-
- I'm sorry.

1243
01:41:18,272 --> 01:41:20,946
It never occurred to me
that you would take it
this hard.

1244
01:41:21,008 --> 01:41:24,649
- I didn't even get
to tell her good-bye.
- Oh, I know.

1245
01:41:24,711 --> 01:41:28,682
These things are difficult,
but she died peacefully
in her sleep.

1246
01:41:28,749 --> 01:41:32,026
To tell you the truth,
I thought you'd be happy
for Mrs. Threadgoode.

1247
01:41:32,085 --> 01:41:35,123
- Happy?
- Why, yes!
This is what she wanted.

1248
01:41:35,188 --> 01:41:37,134
What?
To be dead?

1249
01:41:37,190 --> 01:41:39,727
No, to go home.
You just missed her.

1250
01:41:39,793 --> 01:41:42,239
She left in a yellow cab
about a half hour ago.

1251
01:41:42,296 --> 01:41:45,004
I don't understand.
What? A cab?

1252
01:41:45,065 --> 01:41:49,343
She said there wasn't no
reason for her to stay now
that Mrs. Otis had died.

1253
01:41:49,403 --> 01:41:52,043
Mrs...

1254
01:41:52,105 --> 01:41:54,278
Otis is dead?

1255
01:41:54,341 --> 01:41:58,221
Oh, Mrs. Otis died.

1256
01:41:58,278 --> 01:42:00,280
Mrs. Otis died!

1257
01:42:00,347 --> 01:42:03,556
Mrs. Otis!
Oh, God!

1258
01:42:03,617 --> 01:42:07,656
Not that... I'm glad that
Mrs. Otis died, it's just-

1259
01:42:07,721 --> 01:42:10,361
Oh, God.
I've gotta stop her.

1260
01:42:49,796 --> 01:42:53,039
Hey, Evelyn,
somebody stole my house.

1261
01:42:53,100 --> 01:42:56,013
It was right here
when I left.

1262
01:42:56,069 --> 01:43:00,848
Unless- Oh, Evelyn,
you don't reckon
I'm crazy, do you?

1263
01:43:00,907 --> 01:43:05,117
- It was here
when I left.
- No, honey,
you're not crazy.

1264
01:43:05,178 --> 01:43:07,954
This is the place.

1265
01:43:08,015 --> 01:43:12,054
Why would anyone want to
steal an old lady's home?

1266
01:43:12,119 --> 01:43:14,258
Wasn't worth nothin'.

1267
01:43:14,321 --> 01:43:17,734
Oh, honey,
nobody stole it.

1268
01:43:17,791 --> 01:43:21,671
They had to tear it down.
It was condemned.

1269
01:43:21,728 --> 01:43:23,867
I'm sorry.
I shoulda told you.

1270
01:43:23,930 --> 01:43:27,207
Well, somebody
shoulda told me.

1271
01:43:27,267 --> 01:43:32,114
- I'm old.
I'm not a child.
- I'm sorry.

1272
01:43:32,172 --> 01:43:35,517
My husband Cleo and I
lived in this house...

1273
01:43:35,575 --> 01:43:38,078
for more than 40 years.

1274
01:43:38,145 --> 01:43:41,558
Now, it's... it's gone.

1275
01:43:41,615 --> 01:43:45,188
83 years worth of livin'
and all that's left of me...

1276
01:43:45,252 --> 01:43:49,291
is what's in this box, a
bunch of old cards and pictures.

1277
01:43:49,356 --> 01:43:51,836
Come on.
I'll take you home.

1278
01:43:51,892 --> 01:43:54,031
This is my home!

1279
01:43:54,094 --> 01:43:56,096
And now it's gone.

1280
01:43:56,163 --> 01:43:58,700
And Mrs. Otis
is gone.

1281
01:43:58,765 --> 01:44:00,870
I...

1282
01:44:00,934 --> 01:44:03,540
I don't quite
know what to do.

1283
01:44:03,603 --> 01:44:07,449
This is the first time
I can remember when I don't
have a soul to look after.

1284
01:44:07,507 --> 01:44:09,885
You can come
look after me and Ed.

1285
01:44:09,943 --> 01:44:12,253
Oh, you're sweet,

1286
01:44:12,312 --> 01:44:15,122
but I think you're doin'
just fine on your own.

1287
01:44:15,182 --> 01:44:19,494
Don't you know you'd be
like a gift for us?

1288
01:44:19,553 --> 01:44:22,727
You're the reason
I get up every morning...

1289
01:44:22,789 --> 01:44:26,134
and that Mary Kay's
havin' such a good year...

1290
01:44:26,193 --> 01:44:30,767
and I don't look like some
blob from a horror movie.

1291
01:44:30,831 --> 01:44:34,870
Well,with a little help
from Idgie and Ruth.

1292
01:44:36,436 --> 01:44:38,973
Come on. I've got
your room all ready.

1293
01:44:39,039 --> 01:44:41,451
What does Ed say
about all this?

1294
01:44:41,508 --> 01:44:45,354
He'll learn
to love it.

1295
01:44:48,815 --> 01:44:52,957
Did I ever tell you
that Mrs. Otis was
Sipsey's baby sister?

1296
01:44:53,019 --> 01:44:55,693
- No, ma'am.
- Yes, she was.

1297
01:44:55,755 --> 01:44:59,635
Mrs. Otis was with
Sipsey and me the
night Sipsey died.

1298
01:45:00,713 --> 01:45:04,213
[Edit: Sipsey’s story of the night Frank disappeared]

1299
01:45:17,928 --> 01:45:21,466
- Hey there!
- You got to come quick.

1300
01:45:21,532 --> 01:45:26,504
- The show has hardly begun.
- You got to come quick.
You hear me?

1301
01:45:32,409 --> 01:45:35,015
- Run, get help!
Run, quick!
- Where's the baby?

1302
01:45:35,079 --> 01:45:36,888
Never mind.

1303
01:45:55,599 --> 01:45:57,272
Excuse me, sir.

1304
01:45:57,334 --> 01:46:02,841
I don't believe you
should be goin' anywhere
with Ruth's baby.

1305
01:46:14,485 --> 01:46:17,227
Like I said,
you ain't goin' nowhere.

1306
01:46:17,287 --> 01:46:19,858
Damn, you a thickheaded
son-of-a-bitch, ain't you?

1307
01:46:24,061 --> 01:46:26,041
I told you...

1308
01:46:26,096 --> 01:46:30,545
you ain't goin' nowheres
with Miss Ruth's baby.

1309
01:46:36,173 --> 01:46:38,380
Come on, angel.
Come on.

1310
01:46:38,442 --> 01:46:42,288
Come on, sweetheart.
It's all right.

1311
01:46:42,346 --> 01:46:44,849
Come on.
It's all right, baby.

1312
01:46:47,751 --> 01:46:50,493
it was self-defense.

1313
01:46:50,554 --> 01:46:55,401
I don't know why any
white jury would care
why I did it.

1314
01:46:55,459 --> 01:46:58,269
- Well, I saw it,
and I can testify.
- Excuse me here.

1315
01:46:58,328 --> 01:47:00,501
I don't mean
no offense here,

1316
01:47:00,564 --> 01:47:03,636
but I don't know who's less
likely to convince a jury,

1317
01:47:03,700 --> 01:47:05,976
my mama...
or Mr. Smokey.

1318
01:47:06,036 --> 01:47:08,846
No offense taken.

1319
01:47:08,906 --> 01:47:11,318
You're a good man,
Mr. Smokey.

1320
01:47:11,375 --> 01:47:15,414
- You did good.
- The sun's almost up.

1321
01:47:18,949 --> 01:47:22,328
- George?
- Mm-hmm?

1322
01:47:22,386 --> 01:47:25,162
I think...

1323
01:47:25,222 --> 01:47:28,760
it's hog-boiling time.

1324
01:47:28,825 --> 01:47:31,101
No, ma'am. It
ain't cold enough.

1325
01:47:31,161 --> 01:47:33,937
It's hog-boiling time.

1326
01:47:36,867 --> 01:47:38,813
Big George?

1327
01:47:38,869 --> 01:47:41,975
- Uh-huh?
- When is that barbecue
gonna be ready?

1328
01:47:42,039 --> 01:47:44,383
It's gonna be ready
any time now.

1329
01:47:44,441 --> 01:47:49,356
Smells so damn good I just
can't wait to get me some.

1330
01:47:49,413 --> 01:47:53,725
- Now, don't you forget
to call me when that's ready.
- All right.

1331
01:48:07,464 --> 01:48:09,740
Here you go.

1332
01:48:11,301 --> 01:48:14,942
- Miss Idgie?
Smokey left town.
- Yeah?

1333
01:48:15,005 --> 01:48:19,010
I thought it'd be best
under the circumstances.

1334
01:48:19,076 --> 01:48:23,047
He asked that
you tell Ruth good-bye.

1335
01:48:23,113 --> 01:48:25,593
Shame he had to go.

1336
01:48:32,556 --> 01:48:37,471
Hold on! I'm comin'.

1337
01:48:42,332 --> 01:48:45,108
- What you want?
- We want some barbecue.

1338
01:48:45,168 --> 01:48:48,877
Not today you don't.
Go on.

1339
01:49:01,918 --> 01:49:05,058
Why, this is about the
best barbecue I ever ate!

1340
01:49:06,556 --> 01:49:10,060
The secret's
in the sauce.

1341
01:49:18,835 --> 01:49:22,715
Sipsey?
My God!

1342
01:49:26,979 --> 01:49:28,178
[Edit: “Did Idgie really barbecue Frank?” / why she had to go on trial]

1343
01:49:28,228 --> 01:49:31,641
about what the most
important thing in life is.

1344
01:49:31,698 --> 01:49:34,042
- Do you know
what I think it is?
- No, ma'am.

1345
01:49:34,100 --> 01:49:37,377
Friends.
Best friends.

1346
01:49:37,437 --> 01:49:40,475
Oh. Ninny!

1347
01:49:41,641 --> 01:49:43,382
Look.

1348
01:49:48,648 --> 01:49:50,491
Oh!

1349
01:50:09,702 --> 01:50:11,648
Idgie?

1350
01:50:15,108 --> 01:50:18,988
- Idgie's alive?
- Oh, yes!

1351
01:50:19,045 --> 01:50:23,323
She's still out and about
Charmin' bees and selling honey.

1352
01:50:23,383 --> 01:50:27,354
Sometimes I think
I catch a glimpse of her.

1353
01:50:33,259 --> 01:50:35,705
Maybe we'll
see her today.

1354
01:50:35,762 --> 01:50:38,402
Maybe.

1355
01:50:40,066 --> 01:50:42,774
Let's go.

1356
01:50:54,280 --> 01:50:58,592
After Ruth died and
the railroad stopped runnin',

1357
01:50:58,651 --> 01:51:02,656
the cafe shut down, and everybody
just scattered to the winds.

1358
01:51:03,990 --> 01:51:07,369
It was never more than just
a little knockabout place.

1359
01:51:07,427 --> 01:51:10,237
But now that
I look back on it,

1360
01:51:10,296 --> 01:51:12,572
when that cafe closed...

1361
01:51:12,632 --> 01:51:16,739
the heart of the town
just stopped beating.

1362
01:51:16,803 --> 01:51:19,647
It's funny how
a little place like this...

1363
01:51:19,706 --> 01:51:23,552
brought so

